In ethosu_gem_cmdstream_copy_and_validate(), the loop iterates with 'i < size / 4'. When processing a 64-bit command (cmd & 0x4000), the code increments 'i' and writes to 'bocmds[i]' without checking if the incremented index is still within bounds: 

c
		if (cmd & 0x4000) {
			if (get_user(cmds[1], ucmds++))
				return -EFAULT;

			i++;
			bocmds[i] = cmds[1];
			addr = cmd_to_addr(cmds);
		}


If 'i' is equal to '(size / 4) - 1' at the start of the iteration, 'i++' makes 'i' equal to 'size / 4', leading to an out-of-bounds write at 'bocmds[size / 4]' since the 'bocmds' buffer only has 'size / 4' elements.
